# strict-schema-output-fidelity

When a precise output schema is prescribed, it is a contract, not a template. All output must use exact enum literals, exact formula component names and weights, exact JSON field names, exact data formats (ISO 8601, JSON-only), and verbatim preservation of source field values. No reformatting, synonym substitution, prose wrapping, or 'improvement' of prescribed values is permitted.

## Procedures
- Use only the exact enum literals defined in the schema — never substitute synonyms, capitalization variants, or reformatted equivalents.
- Apply formula components with the exact names and weights prescribed — do not reorder, rename, or adjust weights.
- Output JSON only; never wrap in prose, markdown code fences, or explanation.
- Format all timestamps in ISO 8601 exactly as the schema specifies.
- Preserve original metadata field values verbatim — never reformat, normalize, or 'improve' source values.

## Conventions
- Treat the schema's field names and enum literals as case-sensitive string constants.
- When a schema field has no data, use the schema-prescribed absent marker rather than omitting the field.

